# Force these as binary, always -- never let a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting attempt CRLF<->LF conversion on them. Git's own
# binary-sniffing heuristic happened to save us this time (verified byte-
# for-byte against the committed blobs after a "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" warning on the test corpus's PDFs), but that's git guessing from
# content, not a guarantee — this file makes it a fact, not a heuristic,
# for every contributor's clone regardless of their own git config.
*.pdf   -text
*.docx  -text
*.xlsx  -text
*.xls   -text
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.tiff  -text
*.wav   -text
*.mp3   -text
*.eml   -text
